7	
8	This is the official MCP Server for [HUMAN Security](https://www.humansecurity.com/).
9	
10	# HUMAN Security MCP Server
11	
12	Supercharge your AI workflows with comprehensive cybersecurity intelligence from HUMAN Security. This Model Context Protocol (MCP) server provides access to HUMAN's industry-leading threat detection, attack analysis, and security monitoring capabilities directly within your AI-powered applications.
13	
14	![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HumanSecurity/human-mcp-server/main/.images/mcp.gif)
15	
16	## 🛡️ What You Can Do
17	
18	**Cyberfraud Protection & Analytics**
19	- **Traffic Analysis**: Monitor web and mobile traffic patterns with comprehensive security metrics
20	- **Real-time Attack Monitoring**: Track sophisticated attack campaigns with time-series analytics and threat intelligence
21	- **Attack Investigation**: Deep-dive into specific attack clusters with detailed forensics and attribution
22	- **Account Security**: Investigate suspicious account behavior, fraud patterns, and security incidents
23	- **Custom Security Rules**: Manage and audit your custom mitigation policies and security controls
24	
25	**Code Defender - Client-Side Security**
26	- **Supply Chain Protection**: Monitor third-party scripts and vendors on your payment and sensitive pages
27	- **PCI DSS Compliance**: Automated compliance validation and security assessment for payment environments
28	- **Security Incident Response**: Track client-side attacks, XSS attempts, and code injection threats
29	- **HTTP Security Headers**: Comprehensive security posture analysis and misconfiguration detection
30	
31	## 🚀 Quick Start
32	
33	Add this configuration to your MCP server file:
34	
35	```json
36	{
37	  "mcpServers": {
38	    "human-security": {
39	      "command": "npx",
40	      "args": ["-y", "@humansecurity/human-mcp-server"],
41	      "env": {
42	        "HUMAN_CYBERFRAUD_API_TOKEN": "your-cyberfraud-token",
43	        "HUMAN_CODE_DEFENDER_API_TOKEN": "your-code-defender-token"
44	      }
45	    }
46	  }
47	}
48	```
49	
50	* For Claude Desktop, navigate to **Claude > Settings > Developer > Edit Config**. This will take you to the location of the `claude_desktop_config.json` file. Edit this file in your preferred editor.
51	* For Cursor, navigate to **Cursor > Settings > Cursor Settings > Tools & Integrations**. The MCP Tools section will take you to the `mcp.json` file, which you can edit directly in the Cursor editor.
52	
53	You'll need API tokens from your HUMAN Security account to access the services. The server automatically detects which services you have access to and enables the corresponding tools.
54	
55	### Required Tokens
56	- **`HUMAN_CYBERFRAUD_API_TOKEN`**: Enables attack monitoring, traffic analysis, account investigation, and custom rules management
57	- **`HUMAN_CODE_DEFENDER_API_TOKEN`**: Enables supply chain monitoring, PCI compliance, and client-side security analysis
58	
59	## 🐳 Run with Docker
60	
61	If you prefer Docker over NPM, run the MCP server container directly:
62	
63	```bash
64	docker run --rm -i \
65	  -e HUMAN_CYBERFRAUD_API_TOKEN=<value> \
66	  -e HUMAN_CODE_DEFENDER_API_TOKEN=<value> \
67	  us-docker.pkg.dev/hmn-registry-public/containers/human-mcp-server:latest
68	```
69	
70	To use Docker from your MCP client config (e.g., Cursor or Claude Desktop), replace the NPM command with a Docker invocation:
71	
72	```json
73	{
74	  "mcpServers": {
75	    "human-security": {
76	      "command": "docker",
77	      "args": [
78	        "run", "--rm", "-i",
79	        "-e", "HUMAN_CYBERFRAUD_API_TOKEN",
80	        "-e", "HUMAN_CODE_DEFENDER_API_TOKEN",
81	        "us-docker.pkg.dev/hmn-registry-public/containers/human-mcp-server:latest"
82	      ],
83	      "env": {
84	        "HUMAN_CYBERFRAUD_API_TOKEN": "your-cyberfraud-token",
85	        "HUMAN_CODE_DEFENDER_API_TOKEN": "your-code-defender-token"
86	      }
87	    }
88	  }
89	}
90	```
91	
92	### Optional Configuration
93	- **`HUMAN_API_HOST`**: Use a different API endpoint (default: `api.humansecurity.com`)
94	- **`HUMAN_API_VERSION`**: Specify API version (default: `v1`)
95	- **`HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS`**: Request timeout in milliseconds (default: `30000`)
96	
97	## 💡 Usage Examples
98	
99	**Ask your AI assistant questions like:**
100	
101	* *"Show me attack trends over the last 24 hours"*
102	* *"Investigate suspicious activity for account ID XXXXX"*
103	* *"What third-party scripts are running on our payment pages?"*
104	* *"Are we PCI DSS compliant based on our current security headers?"*
105	* *"Analyze the effectiveness of our custom security rules"*
106	* *"Show me details about attack cluster XXXXX"*
107	
108	## 📊 Available Tools
109	
110	### Cyberfraud Protection
111	- **Traffic Data**: Comprehensive traffic analytics with security metrics
112	- **Attack Reporting (Overtime)**: Time-series attack analytics and trend analysis
113	- **Attack Reporting (Overview)**: Detailed attack cluster intelligence and forensics
114	- **Account Information**: Individual account security analysis and incident tracking
115	- **Custom Rules**: Security policy management and effectiveness analysis
116	
117	### Code Defender Security
118	- **Security Incidents**: Client-side attack detection and investigation
119	- **Script Inventory**: Third-party script monitoring and PCI compliance
120	- **Header Inventory**: HTTP security header analysis and optimization
121	
122	## 🔗 Integration Options
123	
124	### Single Service Setup
125	If you only need one service, you can configure just that token:
126	
127	**Cyberfraud Only:**
128	```json
129	{
130	  "human-security": {
131	    "command": "npx",
132	    "args": ["-y", "@humansecurity/human-mcp-server"],
133	    "env": {
134	      "HUMAN_CYBERFRAUD_API_TOKEN": "your-token-here"
135	    }
136	  }
137	}
138	```
139	
140	**Code Defender Only:**
141	```json
142	{
143	  "human-security": {
144	    "command": "npx",
145	    "args": ["-y", "@humansecurity/human-mcp-server"],
146	    "env": {
147	      "HUMAN_CODE_DEFENDER_API_TOKEN": "your-token-here"
148	    }
149	  }
150	}
151	```
152	
153	## 🆘 Support
154	
155	- **Documentation**: [HUMAN Security Documentation](https://docs.humansecurity.com)
156	- **API Tokens**:
157	  - [Cyberfraud](https://docs.humansecurity.com/applications/reference/authentication#getting-a-token-for-the-account-defender-adaptive-feedback-bot-defender-or-credential-intelligence-api)
158	  - [Code Defender](https://docs.humansecurity.com/applications/reference/authentication#getting-a-token-for-the-code-defender-or-pci-dss-api)
159	- **Technical Support**: Available through your HUMAN Security support channels
